kspec batch cannot handle task patch with nested --data JSON argument. The data object gets stringif
────────────────────────────────────────
ULID:      01KJ4SMATMC7TD3H0C2S5K9W4T
Type:      task
Status:    pending_review
Priority:  3
Automation: eligible

─── Description ───
  kspec batch cannot handle task patch with nested --data JSON argument. The data object gets stringified as [object Object] instead of being serialized as JSON. Batch args are likely passed through a simple string coercion. Workaround: run task patch commands individually. Fix: batch arg handling should JSON.stringify objects before passing to command handlers.
